from flask import Flask, render_template, request
import json

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def index():
    if request.method == 'POST':
        data = request.form.to_dict()
        return json.dumps(data)
    return render_template('index.html')

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

This script creates a simple web application using Flask. When a user visits the homepage, they can fill out a form and submit it. The script will then return the submitted data as JSON.

Remember, it's essential to always obtain user consent before collecting and using their personal information.
